{"skill_id":"first-order-sys","version":1,"questions":[{"id":"first-order-sys-r1-q1","version":1,"round":1,"type":"mc","prompt":"The equation \\(6\\dot{y} + y = 2u\\) is already arranged so the coefficient of \\(y\\) is 1. The time constant, in seconds, is","options":["6","2","1/6","1/3"],"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Once \\(y\\) has coefficient 1, the coefficient of \\(\\dot{y}\\) is the time constant, so \\(\\tau = 6\\). The 2 is the DC gain. \\(1/6\\) is the pole location's magnitude, and \\(2/6\\) divides the gain by the time constant, which is the initial slope for a unit step, not \\(\\tau\\).","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>a first-order rise</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,127.8 52,122.9 55.1,118.4 58.1,114 61.1,109.9 64.1,106.1 67.2,102.4 70.2,99 73.2,95.7 76.2,92.6 79.2,89.7 82.3,86.9 85.3,84.3 88.3,81.8 91.3,79.4 94.4,77.2 97.4,75.1 100.4,73.1 103.4,71.3 106.4,69.5 109.5,67.8 112.5,66.2 115.5,64.7 118.5,63.3 121.6,61.9 124.6,60.7 127.6,59.5 130.6,58.3 133.6,57.2 136.7,56.2 139.7,55.3 142.7,54.3 145.7,53.5 148.8,52.7 151.8,51.9 154.8,51.2 157.8,50.5 160.8,49.8 163.9,49.2 166.9,48.6 169.9,48.1 172.9,47.5 176,47 179,46.6 182,46.1 185,45.7 188,45.3 191.1,44.9 194.1,44.6 197.1,44.3 200.1,43.9 203.2,43.6 206.2,43.4 209.2,43.1 212.2,42.8 215.2,42.6 218.3,42.4 221.3,42.1 224.3,41.9 227.3,41.7 230.4,41.6 233.4,41.4 236.4,41.2 239.4,41.1 242.4,40.9 245.5,40.8 248.5,40.7 251.5,40.5 254.5,40.4 257.6,40.3 260.6,40.2 263.6,40.1 266.6,40 269.6,39.9 272.7,39.8 275.7,39.8 278.7,39.7 281.7,39.6 284.8,39.6 287.8,39.5 290.8,39.4 293.8,39.4 296.8,39.3 299.9,39.3 302.9,39.2 305.9,39.2 308.9,39.1 312,39.1 315,39.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that rises toward a horizontal line."},{"id":"first-order-sys-r1-q2","version":1,"round":1,"type":"numeric","prompt":"The plant \\(6\\dot{y} + y = 2u\\) starts at rest. The input steps to 4 and stays there. The steady output is","answer":8.0,"unit":"1","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"At steady state the derivative is zero, so \\(y = 2u = 2 \\times 4 = 8\\). The 6 never enters the steady value. Dividing the gain by 6 gives \\(4/3\\), and multiplying the input by 6 gives 24.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>step of a first-order plant</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,127.8 52,122.9 55.1,118.4 58.1,114 61.1,109.9 64.1,106.1 67.2,102.4 70.2,99 73.2,95.7 76.2,92.6 79.2,89.7 82.3,86.9 85.3,84.3 88.3,81.8 91.3,79.4 94.4,77.2 97.4,75.1 100.4,73.1 103.4,71.3 106.4,69.5 109.5,67.8 112.5,66.2 115.5,64.7 118.5,63.3 121.6,61.9 124.6,60.7 127.6,59.5 130.6,58.3 133.6,57.2 136.7,56.2 139.7,55.3 142.7,54.3 145.7,53.5 148.8,52.7 151.8,51.9 154.8,51.2 157.8,50.5 160.8,49.8 163.9,49.2 166.9,48.6 169.9,48.1 172.9,47.5 176,47 179,46.6 182,46.1 185,45.7 188,45.3 191.1,44.9 194.1,44.6 197.1,44.3 200.1,43.9 203.2,43.6 206.2,43.4 209.2,43.1 212.2,42.8 215.2,42.6 218.3,42.4 221.3,42.1 224.3,41.9 227.3,41.7 230.4,41.6 233.4,41.4 236.4,41.2 239.4,41.1 242.4,40.9 245.5,40.8 248.5,40.7 251.5,40.5 254.5,40.4 257.6,40.3 260.6,40.2 263.6,40.1 266.6,40 269.6,39.9 272.7,39.8 275.7,39.8 278.7,39.7 281.7,39.6 284.8,39.6 287.8,39.5 290.8,39.4 293.8,39.4 296.8,39.3 299.9,39.3 302.9,39.2 305.9,39.2 308.9,39.1 312,39.1 315,39.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that rises toward a horizontal line."},{"id":"first-order-sys-r1-q3","version":1,"round":1,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A first-order step response starts at rest. At \\(t\\) equal to one time constant, what fraction of the steady value has been reached?","answer":0.632121,"unit":"1","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"From rest, \\(y(t) = y_\\infty(1 - e^{-t/\\tau})\\). At \\(t = \\tau\\) the exponent is \\(-1\\), so the fraction is \\(1 - e^{-1} = 0.632\\). Half would be a different definition. \\(e^{-1} = 0.368\\) is the fraction still missing, and \\(1 - e^{-2}\\) is two time constants.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>one time constant of rise</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"4